// A place the host says is full refuses through the world's `crowded`,
// which `sprout.World` writes as a default and a world may replace, said
// with `{item}` and `{to}` bound: the person turned away, and the place.
// The host's `peoplePerPlace` decides when; `sprout check` runs at the
// defaults, where no place is ever full, so this pins only that the line
// is the world's to write.
world crowded is sprout.World {
  visitors are Person
  visitors arrive at yard

  passage crowded { {to} has no room left for {item}. }

  object yard is sprout.Place
  object shed is sprout.Place
}
